---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Cookie policy" metaTitle="Cookie Policy | SpiceVacations" description="Which cookies and browser storage SpiceVacations.com uses, including analytics and Google advertising cookies, why, and how to change your choice at any time." updated="October 5, 2026">
  <p>We use as little tracking as possible. Here's exactly what we use and how to control it.</p>
  <h2>Essential storage (always on)</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>sv:consent</td><td>Local storage</td><td>Remembers your cookie choice</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
      <tr><td>sv:saved</td><td>Local storage</td><td>Keeps your saved trips on this device</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h2>Analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
  <p>If you choose "Accept all," we may load privacy-focused analytics (such as Plausible and/or Google Analytics 4) to measure page visits and events like searches, planner submissions, newsletter sign-ups and partner clicks. If you choose "Essential only," these scripts never load.</p>
  <h2>Advertising cookies (Google AdSense)</h2>
  <p>
    We may display ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies (such as those set on doubleclick.net and
    googlesyndication.com) to show and measure ads and to prevent fraud. With Google Consent Mode, these cookies are not used for personalized ads
    unless you choose "Accept all." If you choose "Essential only," ads may still appear, but they are non-personalized. You can also manage
    personalized ads at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a> or
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Partner cookies</h2>
  <p>When you click through to a booking partner, that partner may set cookies on its own site to attribute your booking. Those cookies are governed by the partner's policies.</p>
  <h2>Change your choice</h2>
  <p>You can change your choice at any time:</p>
  <p><button class="btn btn--sm" type="button" data-cookie-settings>Open cookie settings</button></p>
</Page>
